Where the code comes from
=========================

pinext is assembled from two bodies of work. This file records both, because the
licence of the whole follows from the stricter of the two.

1. **FastVibe 0.19.5** — https://github.com/tyuan511/fastvibe
   MIT licensed. The original text is kept verbatim in `LICENSE-FASTVIBE-MIT`.
   FastVibe supplied the application as it stands today: the Electron main
   process and engine, the renderer, the headless agent, the mobile client under
   `apps/mobile_flutter`, and the whole `resources/` tree.

2. **Pi Web / PI NEXT** — https://github.com/agegr/pi-web
   Distributed as a whole under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later
   (see `LICENSE`), with `LICENSE-MIT` covering the parts that record their own
   MIT notice, including the upstream project that work is based on.
   PI NEXT is the source of the features this project adds on top of FastVibe:
   document preview and document tools, image generation, the web-search
   provider chain, the IM bridge and inbound bot channels, the automation
   scheduler, the MCP management surface, the git graph, the call-trace view and
   Markdown export. Ported code carries a `fork:` marker naming what it came
   from.

