Third-party binaries fetched at build time
=========================================

The computer-use driver (`@trycua/cua-driver`, fetched by
`scripts/fetch-cua-driver.mjs` into `resources/cua-driver/`) and the remote agent
runtime archives are **not** part of this source tree. Each is pinned and
checksummed by the script that fetches it; see `scripts/`. Their own licences
apply to those artifacts.

---

Services this build deliberately does not use
=============================================

This build does not talk to any upstream service. In particular it does not
contact `fastvibe.dev` / `app.fastvibe.dev` — the upstream account and WebRTC
relay — and it does not use the upstream GitHub repository as an update feed or
as a download source for remote agent runtimes. Those are replaced by the
operator's own service (see `docs/pinext-cloud-contract-2026-10-13.md`) or left
unconfigured, in which case the corresponding feature reports itself as disabled
instead of failing against a stranger's host.
